> roidesfoux wrote:
> > > I don't know if Slash'em is akin to vanilla in this regard, but in
> > > vanilla throwing Mjollnir is a _very_ bad idea as it has a tendency to
> > > blow up any rings/wands you have in open inventory (including worn
> > > rings).  IMO being able to throw Mojo is a devteam trap.
> > I find this VERY odd, as I've ascended at least one Valk in vanilla.
> > For most of the game, she was wearing two rings, with multiple wands in
> > her inventory, and was pitching Mojo left and right. The hammer never
> > destroyed any of my items.
> You got lucky.  It happens.  It's about 1% chance every time you throw
> it that you won't catch it; then there's a chance it lands at your
> feet. If it hits you, there's a chance for every ring/wand in you
> inventory to be destroyed.

Feet/hit distribution should be 50/50 if it is the same as in vanilla.

So, a 1/200 chance of it hitting you (if you're a Valkyrie, otherwise no 
return of course).

That's if you're not confused, stunned, blind, hallucinating or 
fumbling, because then there is no chance of catching it, just the 50/50 
chance of feet/hit.
 
> If you toss it with any regularity, over the course of a full game
> there's a good chance you'll blow some stuff up.

It would be interesting to know how the chance of destroying each 
ring/wand is calculated, to see what the total risk is. But IANASD 
tonight.

